.TH WISIRC 1 "2026-10-28" "wisirc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wisirc \- terminal IRC client with mouse, menus and a live dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wisirc
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-copy\fR \fIpath\fR]
.br
.B wisirc \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wisirc
is an IRC client for the terminal. It connects to several servers at once
(TLS and SASL PLAIN), shows them in a sidebar with their channels, a chat
panel and a nick list, and can be used entirely with the mouse (clicks,
wheel, context menus) or entirely with the keyboard.
.PP
It starts on a dashboard with one card per server: connection state,
uptime, an animated lag graph, joined channels and unread messages.
The interface is available in English and Spanish.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the configuration from \fIfile\fR instead of
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wisirc/config.toml\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-copy " path"
Copy an existing config to the config file (and the directory it is in),
then start with it. \fIpath\fR is a wisirc config directory or
\fIconfig.toml\fR (its \fIservers.toml\fR and \fIprefs.toml\fR come
along), or a Halloy \fIconfig.toml\fR or directory (its servers are
imported into \fIservers.toml\fR). Nothing is ever replaced: if the
destination already has a config, wisirc prints an error and exits. The
copies are readable only by their owner. The first-run setup is skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Each server is a TOML table:
.PP
.nf
.RS
[servers.libera]
  nickname = "alice"
  server = "irc.libera.chat"
  port = 6697
  channels = ["#wisirc"]

  [servers.libera.sasl.plain]
  username = "alice"
  password = "secret"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Other keys: \fBusername\fR, \fBrealname\fR, \fBuse_tls\fR (on by default
on port 6697), \fBpassword\fR (server or bouncer password),
\fBdangerously_accept_invalid_certs\fR, \fBautoconnect\fR.
Servers saved or edited from inside wisirc go to \fIservers.toml\fR, which
wins over this file for the same name; choices made in the menus (theme,
language, server colors, disabled servers) go to \fIprefs.toml\fR, both
next to the configuration file.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F1
Main menu (also a click on \fB≡\fR).
.TP
.B F2
Dashboard (also a click on the \fBwisirc\fR title).
.TP
.B Alt+1..9, Ctrl+N, Ctrl+P
Switch buffers.
.TP
.B Alt+A
Next buffer with activity, mentions first.
.TP
.B PgUp, PgDn
Scroll the history.
.TP
.B Tab
Complete a nick.
.TP
.B Esc
Close a menu, panel or screen.
.SH COMMANDS
.BR /connect " (" /conectar ") \fIname\fR | \fIhost\fR [\fIport\fR] [\fB\-nick\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB\-user\fR \fIu\fR] [\fB\-pass\fR \fIp\fR] [\fB\-sasl\fR \fIuser:pass\fR] [\fB\-join\fR \fI#a,#b\fR] [\fB\-tls\fR|\fB\-notls\fR] [\fB\-insecure\fR] [\fB\-name\fR \fIn\fR]"
.br
Without arguments it opens a screen with examples.
.PP
.BR /join ", " /part ", " /msg ", " /query ", " /me ", " /nick ", " /whois ", " /topic ", " /kick ", " /ban ", " /mode ", " /quote ", " /close ", " /quit
.br
The usual IRC commands.
.PP
.BR /theme " (" /tema ") [\fIname\fR], " /lang " (" /idioma ") [\fBen\fR|\fBes\fR], " /panel ", " /help
.PP
.BR /export " (" /exportar ") " halloy " [\fIfile\fR]"
.br
Writes the saved servers as a Halloy config, passwords included, to
\fIfile\fR or to \fIhalloy-export.toml\fR next to the config. The file is
created with mode 0600 and an existing file is never replaced.
.PP
.BR /update " (" /actualizar )
.br
Installs the newest release over this binary (checked against its
SHA256SUMS); it is used the next time wisirc starts. wisirc looks for new
releases on GitHub at startup and once a day; turn that off with
\fBcheck = false\fR under \fB[updates]\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wisirc/config.toml
Configuration written by hand.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wisirc/servers.toml
Servers saved or edited from the Servers screen.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wisirc/prefs.toml
Identity (nick and real name from the first-run setup), theme, language,
server colors and disabled servers chosen in the menus.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/wisirc/logs/
One folder per server and buffer, one file per day.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANG, LC_MESSAGES, LC_ALL
Pick the default language (Spanish for es_*, English otherwise).
.TP
.B COLORTERM
\fBtruecolor\fR or \fB24bit\fR forces 24-bit color.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME
Base folders for configuration and logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR irssi (1)
.PP
https://github.com/eddyv73/wisirc
